# Payment security

A payment is real only after the server verifies a signed provider notice.

- Keep raw card numbers and track data out of the process.
- Treat a button press, a query flag, or a client status as untrusted.
- Apply each provider event id once.
- Expire unpaid sessions and release their stock.
- Refuse a provider whose mode is not `simulation` until a live verifier exists.

```ts
const notice = provider.verify(body, signature);
if (seen.has(notice.providerEventId)) return order;
```

Do not store a secret in the repository. Do not describe a generic NFC reader as a contactless card terminal.
